	(text "C = 1/(n * pi * f_receiver_bandwidth * R) = ~87nF -> 82nF\n(82 is a standard value)\n\n\nWhere n is one over the fraction of time each cap is \ncharging, 2 in our case of a double balanced detector\n\nR is the impedence (50 ohms)\n\nf_receiver_bandwidth is the target bandwidth (32kHz)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 201.676 122.174 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "05682a4a-9530-4f06-a955-df88946b9ac5")
	)
	(text "32kHz comes from the fact that AM signals are\nat 10kHz channel widths, so 32kHz fits -16kHz to 16kHz, \ncomfortably in the margin of applying an even\nfilter on it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 202.692 204.47 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "150a82be-1bf6-43e2-be94-38bd651aaa7c")
	)
	(text "Have channels A and B always\nactive by pulling low"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 81.534 200.406 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "31fd89e7-041c-480f-9d60-c88d28052111")
	)
	(text "Decoupling Caps"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 276.86 189.992 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "3cb1ed72-ed91-4787-acc0-db3767d9e7d3")
	)
	(text "Both RF and ~RF are biased to 1.65V DC and\nare the raw rf waveforms after the LPF\n\nThe only difference is that ~RF is inverted\n\nThe purpose of this is to minimize loss\nby implementing a double-balanced \nTayloe Detector."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 252.73 56.896 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "44cbc73a-741f-4f67-b30d-aa18f63c2758")
	)
	(text "(optional)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 351.79 133.604 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "44d6d7ca-c08a-4b2f-a33c-27db254894c1")
	)
	(text "Gain should be roughly 24 V/V\n\nV_out = 1.65 + (4.99k / 210) x (V+ - V-)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 324.104 216.662 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "49244610-16ad-4e63-84f0-6002a4ea9790")
	)
	(text "Dual-Channel Differential Amplifier\nfor getting the In-Phase (I) and\nQuadrature (Q) signals from the mixer\nand sending to STM32 for sampling"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 326.898 204.47 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "4cf98b93-3dea-4359-9f9f-37a1c9b2c89b")
	)
	(text "forms a basic RC filter with corner frequency around 18kHz\n\nC is 1.8nF\nR is 4.99k\n\nC=1/(2pi * R * f)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 328.168 113.792 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "50e45a1b-24d6-471d-a699-0fe458fd049c")
	)
	(text "PI3B3253QEX-2017 dual channel 1:4 multiplexer"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 81.788 196.088 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "70462161-74ed-4a6f-8af9-93b139088c66")
	)
	(text "\"magnitude response of a first-order (RC) lowpass filter\"\n\n|H(f)| = 1/sqrt(1 + (f/f_bandwidth)^2)\n\n|H(f)| tells us the proportion of the signal\nallowed through at a certain frequency depending\non the set bandwidth of the filter"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 201.676 220.98 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "7704c31e-24c8-49cb-82a6-70f01f614c36")
	)
